---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Use Cases | BeaconGuard Consequential AI Authorization"
  description="BeaconGuard use cases for independently authorizing exact consequential AI actions in healthcare, financial services, and regulated internal automation."
>
  <section>
    <h1>Use Cases</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      BeaconGuard is for workflows where AI can do more than generate content. The relevant boundary appears when an agent can create a consequential side effect in an enterprise system or external interaction.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Priority workflow patterns</h2>
    <div class="section-grid">
      <div class="content-card">
        <h3>Healthcare operational actions</h3>
        <p>Patient communication, scheduling, operational record updates, and bounded discharge operations where the exact side effect must be authorized without replacing clinical or EHR authority.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="content-card">
        <h3>Financial workflow actions</h3>
        <p>AML/KYC, fraud, dispute, case-state, customer communication, and other customer-impacting actions where broad system access should not equal blanket action authority.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="content-card">
        <h3>Regulated internal automation</h3>
        <p>Agents changing production systems, configurations, records, or external communications under exact-action, one-time, fail-closed authorization.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Use-case selection test</h2>
    <p>A strong BeaconGuard use case has four properties:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>An AI or agent can propose or initiate a concrete side effect.</li>
      <li>The side effect is consequential enough that broad access alone is insufficient.</li>
      <li>Customer policy, approval, identity, delegation, or context should determine whether it may occur.</li>
      <li>The organization benefits from reconstructing what action was authorized under which policy authority.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Not the target problem</h2>
    <p>
      BeaconGuard is not primarily a prompt filter, chatbot guardrail, model-evaluation platform, AI inventory, or general GRC repository. Those products may remain complementary. BeaconGuard's focus is the authorization boundary immediately before consequential execution.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Explore</h2>
    <div class="page-actions">
      <a class="btn-primary" href="/canonical-workflow">Review Workflow Examples</a>
      <a class="btn-secondary" href="/healthcare">Healthcare</a>
      <a class="btn-secondary" href="/fintech">Financial</a>
      <a class="btn-secondary" href="/design-partner-program">Controlled Evaluation</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
